-- title:
--   Anemic and full local Hecke algebras agree at ρ̄
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}$, let $p\neq 2$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$: a $k$-space $V$ of rank $2$ with a multiplicative map $\rho$ from the group of $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb{Q}$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ that is trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, assumed absolutely irreducible (the base change to $\overline{k}$ has no invariant submodule besides $\bot$ and $\top$). Let $S_0\subseteq S$ be finite sets of naturals with all elements of $S$ prime and $p\in S$, and $N\neq 0$ with every prime divisor in $S$ and outside $S_0$, $p^2\nmid N$. The local conditions are: $\bar\rho$ is unramified at each $q\in S$, $q\neq p$, $q\nmid N$ (i.e. $\rho$ is trivial on the inertia subgroup of every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit); for $q\neq p$ prime with $q\Vert N$, $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ and every inertia element at $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$; for $q\neq p$ prime with $q^2\mid N$, $q^3\nmid N$ and inertia at $q$ is again unipotent in that sense; and if $p\mid N$ then $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$, meaning that for each $P$ over $p$ there is a line $L=\mathcal{O}\!\cdot\! b_0$ spanned by a basis vector, stable under the decomposition group, with $\rho(\sigma)v-v\in L$ for all $\sigma$ in inertia and all $v$. Assume weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb{C}$ by forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients. Let $\theta'$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S_0$) and the $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid N$, $q\notin S_0$), subject to: for primes $\ell\neq p$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S_0$, and any valuation subring $P$ over $\ell$ and any $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, $\mathrm{charpoly}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)=X^2-\theta'(T_\ell)X+\ell$; $\theta'(U_q)=0$ when $q\mid N$, $q\notin S_0$ and $q^2\mid N$; $\theta'(U_q)$ equals the trace of any $k$-endomorphism of $V/\sum_{\tau\in I_P}\mathrm{range}(\rho(\tau)-1)$ induced by a Frobenius $\sigma$ at $q$, when $q\mid N$, $q\notin S_0$, $q^2\nmid N$; and likewise $\theta'(T_p)$ equals such a trace at $p$ when $p\nmid N$ and $p\notin S_0$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $k$ obtained from $\theta'$ by composing with the inclusion of Hecke algebras induced by $S_0\subseteq S$, and let $\Psi$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map from [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) to [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S₀ 𝒪 θ'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) (the localisations at the primes cut out by $\theta$, $\theta'$) commuting with the structural maps $\pi$ from the respective Hecke algebras along that inclusion. Then $\Psi$ is bijective.
--
--   This is the identification of the Hecke algebra away from $S$ with the Hecke algebra away from the smaller set $S_0$, after localisation at the maximal ideal attached to $\bar\rho$ at a level $N$ of type $\Sigma$ for $\bar\rho$ (Darmon–Diamond–Taylor, Proposition 4.7; Wiles, Proposition 2.15): at such a level the extra operators $T_q,U_q$ for $q\in S\setminus S_0$ bring nothing new locally. It feeds the construction of an isomorphism of the local Hecke algebra with the ring appearing in the numerical criterion, via [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algEquiv_sigmaCornerRing_auxLevel`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algEquiv_sigmaCornerRing_auxLevel).
